{
  "dom_id": "step-q66556",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "${3}^{0}=1$ can be expressed as",
  "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${3}^{0}=1$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=1,b=3$ and $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the equation ${3}^{0}=1$ is equivalent to ${log}_{3}⁡1=0.$\n\nNote that ${log}_{n}⁡1=0$ for any $n>0,n\\ne 1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
